course: dictionary
lesson: 12506
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word deployment is a good example. «The deployment of the troops took three days.» The clues troops and days tell you it means sending soldiers to a place.
explain: «The airbag deployment saved the driver from injury.» Now the word airbag tells you that deployment means an airbag opening up fast in a crash. Read the words around the word first, then check that your meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Families of soldiers often say «my dad is on deployment». This means he has been sent away to serve somewhere for a time. The phrase is about a person being away, so the words around it are your clue.
fact: Deployment is a noun. You can say a deployment, or several deployments.
fact: Deployment can mean sending soldiers, ships or equipment to a place so they are ready to act.
fact: Deployment can also mean putting something into use, such as a parachute opening.
fact: «Airbag deployment» means an airbag inflating in a crash.
fact: «On deployment» means a soldier has been sent away to serve for a time.
exercise: «The deployment of ships to the coast took two weeks.» What does deployment mean here? | Selling old boats | A holiday trip by boat | Building a new harbour | *Sending ships to a place so they are ready to act
exercise: «The airbag deployment in the crash saved the driver.» What does deployment mean here? | A crash test that failed | A car being sold | A bag of sweets | *An airbag opening up fast
exercise: Ella says «my dad is on deployment». What does on deployment mean? | Sleeping in a tent on holiday | Lost in a forest | At home, resting after work | *Sent away to serve somewhere for a time
test: «The software deployment went live on Monday.» What does deployment mean here? | Writing a letter about computers | Turning the screen off for a rest | Breaking the computer on purpose | *Releasing new software for people to use
test: Mum says «Dad's deployment ends in May.» What does deployment mean here? | A map of the country | A birthday party for Dad | A new job at home | *A time when Dad is away serving
exam: Which meaning of deployment fits best in «The parachute deployment was perfect, and the jumper floated safely down»? | A time spent away from home | *Putting it into use, by opening the parachute | Sending soldiers to a place | Packing a bag for a trip
